        "## 🏗️ Constructor in Python (__init__)\n",
        "📌 What is a Constructor?\n",
        "\n",
        "A constructor is a special method that is automatically called when an object is created.\n",
        "\n",
        "In Python, the constructor is defined using:\n",
        "init()\n",
        "\n",
        " It is also called the initializer method."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ywzPhTPvyTI9"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 🔑 Purpose of __init__\n",
        "- Initialize object attributes\n",
        "- Assign values when an object is created\n",
        "- Set default or custom data"
