        "## Methods in OOP (Python)\n",
        "\n",
        "In Object-Oriented Programming, methods are functions defined inside a class that describe the behavior of objects.\n",
        "\n",
        "👉 **In simple words**:\n",
        "- A method = function that belongs to a class"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3PvcS3hWMhVr"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Types of Methods in Python\n",
        "1. **Instance Methods**\n",
        "2. **Class Methods**\n",
        "3. **Static Methods**\n",
        "\n",
        "## Instance Methods\n",
        "- Work with object data\n",
        "- Use self parameter\n",
        "- Most commonly used"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DfwRFqwhQQHv"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Instance Method\n",
        "class Student:\n",
        "  schoolname = \"XYZ SCHOOL\"\n",
        "  def __init__(self,name,marks):\n",
        "    self.name = name\n",
        "    self.marks = marks\n",
        "\n",
        "  # Instance/Object method always take self as a argument\n",
        "  def displayinfo(self): # Instance Method\n",
        "    print(f\"Student name is {self.name} and he/she got {self.marks} marks\")\n",
        "\n",
        "  def get_marks(self): # Instance Method\n",
        "    return self.marks\n",
        "\n",
        "s1 =Student('kamil',90)\n",
        "s1.displayinfo()\n",
        "print(s1.get_marks())"
