      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 2. 📘 Class Method\n",
        " 🧠 Concept\n",
        "\n",
        "A class method is a method that:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Works with the class itself (not individual objects)\n",
        "- Uses cls instead of self\n",
        "- Defined using @classmethod\n",
        "\n",
        "👉 It is mainly used to access or modify class variables"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BIKjUkKcc1ta"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "class Student:\n",
        "    school_name = \"Aitchison School\"   # class variable\n",
        "\n",
        "    @classmethod\n",
        "    def change_school(cls, name):\n",
        "        cls.school_name = name\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Before change\n",
        "print(Student.school_name)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Change using class method\n",
        "Student.change_school(\" Lead School System \")\n",
        "\n",
        "# After change\n",
        "print(Student.school_name)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Again changing the school name using the class method\n",
        "Student.change_school(\"Ajk School\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Important\n",
        "#  Updating via class method overwrites the previous class variable value\n",
        "\n",
        "print(Student.school_name)\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "Ob_Z4YdDdQPQ",
        "outputId": "b15eeb43-8a07-4f1f-f25f-3903e4a0cf06"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Aitchison School\n",
            " Lead School System \n",
            "Ajk School\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 3. 📘 Static Method in Python (OOP)\n",
        "🧠 Concept\n",
        "\n",
        "A static method is a method that:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Belongs to a class\n",
        "- Does NOT use self (object)\n",
        "- Does NOT use cls (class)\n",
        "- Works like a normal function, but is grouped inside a class\n",
        "\n",
        "👉 It is defined using the decorator: @staticmethod\n",
        "\n",
        "✅ In simple words:\n",
        "\n",
        "\"Put utility/helper functions inside a class for better organization\""
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fkw1ym8EY_7G"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
