        " ## 1️⃣ Abstraction (Hiding Complexity)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Abstraction** is about showing only the necessary details to the user, while hiding internal implementations.\n",
        "\n",
        "In Python, we often implement abstract classes using the abc module."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BKgFCqKonSDJ"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "class Car:\n",
        "    def __init__(self):\n",
        "        # Private attributes hidden from the user\n",
        "        #Private Attribute: A variable in a class that is hidden from outside access to protect the internal state.\n",
        "        self.__accelerator = False\n",
        "        self.__brake = False\n",
        "        self.__clutch = False\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Abstract Method: A method that hides implementation details and exposes only the necessary functionality to the user.\n",
        "    def start(self):\n",
        "        # Abstracted method: user just calls start() without worrying about details\n",
        "        self.__clutch = True\n",
        "        self.__accelerator = True\n",
        "        print(\"Car - Started!\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Using the class\n",
        "c1 = Car()\n",
        "c1.start()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "xL2XJ-UnnpsO",
        "outputId": "e90d0b5b-02cf-4a15-a625-6b9c74179520"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Car - Started!\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 2️⃣ Encapsulation (Data Hiding)\n",
        "\n",
        "Encapsulation is about restricting direct access to some attributes and exposing methods to interact safely with them.\n",
        "- It is basically wrapping data and functions into the single unit (object)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qgt7EvkLnKWy"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Private Attributes:\n",
        "\n",
        "Variables in a class prefixed with __ that cannot be accessed directly from outside of the class , used to hide data and enforce controlled access through methods."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1z1fJuxN5NpU"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Getter Method\n",
        "\n",
        "A getter is a method used to access the value of a private attribute from outside the class.\n",
        "\n",
        "Since private attributes (like __balance) cannot be accessed directly, the getter provides safe read access."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "anflzJkM4-vB"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Setter Method\n",
        "\n",
